1> and\n<MATH_0012> with target <MATH_0013> such that <MATH_0014>\nthere exists an <MATH_0015> with source <MATH_0016> such that\n<MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0003>\nA set of arrows <MATH_0018> of <MATH_0019> is\ncalled a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>right multiplicative system<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif it has the following properties:\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<ITEMOPEN_0004>RMS1<ITEMCLOSE_0004> The identity of every object of <MATH_0020> is in <MATH_0021> and\nthe composition of two composable elements of <MATH_0022> is in <MATH_0023>.\n<ITEMOPEN_0005>RMS2<ITEMCLOSE_0005> Every solid diagram\n<MATH_0024>\nwith <MATH_0025> can be completed to a commutative dotted square with\n<MATH_0026>.\n<ITEMOPEN_0006>RMS3<ITEMCLOSE_0006> For every pair of morphisms <MATH_0027> and\n<MATH_0028> with source <MATH_0029> such that <MATH_0030>\nthere exists a <MATH_0031> with target <MATH_0032> such that\n<MATH_0033>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nA set of arrows <MATH_0034> of <MATH_0035> is called a <TEXTITOPEN_0003>multiplicative system<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nif it is both a left multiplicative system and a right multiplicative system.\nIn other words, this means that MS1, MS2, MS3 hold, where\nMS1 <MATH_0036> LMS1 <MATH_0037> RMS1, MS2 <MATH_0038> LMS2 <MATH_0039> RMS2, and\nMS3 <MATH_0040> LMS3 <MATH_0041> RMS3. (That said, of course LMS1 <MATH_0042> RMS1\n<MATH_0043> MS1.)\n<STRUCT_0006>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa501b163338449061afcd718feb2e482e8e5824bdb0b38c1c3b562b5f6e2bdc", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04VC:definition/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:04VD:lemma/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:f3aba30d4469934f0451fe112ece025196ff212a2afc294dfbec46416a26f4d0", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:04VD:lemma/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 142854, "byte_start": 142401, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:b94265af9514c399fc4950ce05c371ad1b50c5b4c243a27351cbbc6c0c082a8f", "line_end": 4012, "line_start": 4001}, "owner_tag": "04VD", "parent_tag": "04VB", 